          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultanate_of_Rum"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "phase": "zenith",
      "years": "1176–1243",
      "description": "Defeats Byzantine Emperor Manuel I at Myriokephalon (1176), ending Byzantine hopes of reconquering Anatolia; Kilij Arslan II and successors build a prosperous commercial state; Konya becomes a major Silk Road hub and center of Persian Sufi culture (Rumi/Mevlana)",
      "sources": [
        {
          "type": "wikidata",
          "id": "Q975405",
          "url": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q975405"
        },
        {
          "type": "wikipedia",
          "label": "Sultanate of Rum",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultanate_of_Rum"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "phase": "mongol_vassalage",
      "years": "1243–1307",
      "description": "Mongol Ilkhanate crushes the sultanate at Battle of Köse Dağ (1243); sultans become Mongol vassals; authority fragments among competing princes and Mongol-backed governors; Turkic beys establish independent principalities (beyliks) as central control collapses",
      "sources": [
        {
          "type": "wikidata",
          "id": "Q975405",
          "url": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q975405"
        },
        {
